<title>BELGIUM: FRANKI NARROWS 1996 LOSS, NO DIVIDEND.</title>
<headline>FRANKI NARROWS 1996 LOSS, NO DIVIDEND.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31,</p>
<p>1996 (in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net loss		   110  vs     138</p>
<p>    Cons sales/turnover	 10,356  vs  10,908</p>
<p>    Cons operating profit	  107  vs	45</p>
<p>    Cons pre-tax loss		 69  vs	87</p>
<p>    Cash flow			  137  vs     255</p>
<p>    Dividend (francs)		nil  vs     nil</p>
<p>NOTE - Franki is a Belgian construction group with worldwide</p>
<p>interests.</p>
<p>At a news conference, the company said 1996 earnings were</p>
<p>hit by exceptional charges totalling 93.3 million francs linked</p>
<p>to redundancies at its French and U.S. units. The group also</p>
<p>booked a 46.7 million franc charge on the sale of a 25 percent</p>
<p>stake in Germany's Franki Grundbau to Philipp Holzmann .</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
